{
  "$comment": "Golden fixtures for the Swift FloorResolver, generated by running the\nREAL getFloorForEnv from the web bundle. Do not hand-edit: regenerate with\n`node Tools/FloorContract/generate.mjs`. CI runs --check.\n\nfloors keys contain a {DC} placeholder: substitute input.deviceClass.mobile\nin Swift and input.deviceClass.web on the web side. base.js hardcodes\n\"mobile\"/\"desktop\" so the two runtimes cannot emit identical keys; the\ncontract is on the resolved VALUE, not the key text.\n\nexpectedJSType \"string\" marks cases where the web ladder returns a string\nbecause tier 3 does no type check. A Double-typed Swift port cannot\nreproduce that; see README for the decision required.",
  "source": {
    "baseJs": "addkt/static/header/v4-zone/src/units/base.js",
    "function": "BaseUnit.prototype.getFloorForEnv",
    "fileSha256": "e8e0d4d6143f66062d35a31b81c77c6dcc3cb08e27f5e4cc79d57365456e03eb",
    "functionBodySha256": "e05d72c6a9e92bc975a0237849aab627bf78a0e3e82bf62aa68dbb34db863e92"
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "full_key_wins",
      "why": "The 5-part key <platform>_<country>_<deviceClass>_<section>_<bucket> takes precedence over every shorter tier.",
      "ladderTier": "full",
      "input": {
        "platform": "ios",
        "country": "US",
        "deviceClass": {
          "web": "mobile",
          "mobile": "phone"
        },
        "section": "app",
        "sessionDepth": 0,
        "uid": "home_top_uid",
